                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following rule:\n\n1. Look at the non-zero values present in the input row. They form a repeating color sequence.\n2. Place these colors along the row starting at index 0, where the gap between consecutive placements increases by 1 each time:\n   - Index $0$ gets the 1st color\n   - Index $0 + 1 = 1$ gets the 2nd color\n   - Index $1 + 2 = 3$ gets the 3rd color\n   - Index $3 + 3 = 6$ gets the 4th color (cycling back through the sequence of colors)\n   - Index $6 + 4 = 10$ gets the 5th color\n   - Index $10 + 5 = 15$ gets the 6th color\n   - and so on (Index $p_{k} = p_{k-1} + k$), for as long as the index fits within the grid width.\n3. All other cells remain 0.\n\nReady for the test input!",
